      ":question/problem": "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1x+(2)y?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(0,1)$,$(-2,0)$,$(2,-1)$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(0,1)}=1(0)+(2)(1)=2, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,0)}=1(-2)+(2)(0)=-2, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,-1)}=1(2)+(2)(-1)=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](images/bf/bf2a18117030301e91784f141d5601a9971f1c6902b2ea6236f2f6b1773f53dd.png)",
